# Adaptive exploration protocol

The original request is F0. Read configured canonical docs before treating code as authority. Then create `CONTEXT-PLAN`; there is no universal F2 fork.

- `LEXICAL_ENUMERATION`: shard `rg` discovery by non-overlapping filesystem scope; classify; then graph/LSP candidate owners to entrypoints.
- `KNOWN_SYMBOL_IMPACT`: graph ∥ `rg` only for high-radius/completeness work; graph-first plus focused verification for low-radius work.
- `DYNAMIC_STATE_FLOW`: `rg` + focused reads/LSP prove event -> data/state -> behavior; graph follows consumers afterwards.
- `DOCS_OR_CONFIG`: canonical docs + textual search + focused reads.
- `LIVE_STATE`: read-only runtime/database evidence ∥ relevant code; never infer absence from a permission failure.

A stale graph cannot support a completeness claim. Provider capabilities are versioned in `.harness/context-providers/`; limitations from one provider are not universal rules. Record every skipped phase and fallback.
